descriptionByLocale.en:
You want to give meaning to your professional practice by accompanying people in their daily lives, with respect and benevolence. By listening carefully to their needs, you offer appropriate care, both preventive and supportive, and help maintain their autonomy every day.

If these values inspire you and you want to engage in a meaningful mission, this opportunity is for you.

For our Martigny site, we are looking for:

An 80% CASS

About us:

By joining our team, you will not simply be a care professional: you will play a key role in improving the quality of life of our clients. Your mission will be to provide quality care and assistance directly at home.

In addition to the care, you will provide practical daily help, by accompanying our clients in household tasks and everyday activities.

You will work closely with a multidisciplinary team and will actively contribute to the well-being of our clients.

What we are looking for:

* A CCSA CFC or equivalent;
* Experience in the area of home care and assistance would be an asset;
* The ability to work within a multidisciplinary and autonomous team;
* Knowledge of the canton's health, social and voluntary network;
* Reflexivity and adaptability;
* The mastery of common computer tools;
* No one's being transported.

What we offer:

* A varied and meaningful activity in a changing sector;
* A dynamic and collaborative working environment;
* Mobile and modern work tools;
* A work environment that promotes reconciliation between private and professional life;
* opportunities for further training and skills development;
* Attractive social benefits and benefits;
* Working conditions consistent with the LTC SLD.

Don't hesitate! Join us as soon as possible to make your positive contribution and make a difference in the well-being of our customers.

Entry into office: as soon as possible or date to be agreed.

For the sake of inclusiveness, all the male forms used extend to the female as well.

